KNOWNBUG: [temp.inst]/2, [basic.lookup.unqual] -- a class template's out-of-line
member is instantiated with the method scope created under whatever scope first
triggered the instantiation, rather than under the template's own scope, so a
namespace-scope typedef in the member's return type is looked up in the wrong
scope ("symbol 'SID' is unknown").  Reduced from the interval_union.cpp dog-food
failure.  An unconditional fix regresses real-STL instantiations
(std::unordered_map); a narrowly-scoped fix is still needed.  Flip to CORE then.
